Great post, very sad. We should really try to improve reproducibility. Gabriele Berton commits to never hire anyone with over 50% of their papers not fully reproducible, based on GitHub issues and code being released by conference date.

@ChenhaoTan: "How much science is verifiable? Results from replicating ICML 2026 oral papers."

As AI agents become capable of increasingly complex, long-horizon tasks, we have an exciting opportunity to rethink the research.
